cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Toward Appraisal-Structured Latent Control Representations in Language Models: A Preregistered Hypothesis and Experimental Design for Task-Induced Response-Strategy Modulation"
abstract: >-
  A preregistered hypothesis and experimental-design note proposing that several
  known single-behavior latent directions in language models (refusal, abstention,
  uncertainty reporting, evaluation awareness) may be special cases of a more
  general family of task-induced, appraisal-structured latent control
  representations that partially govern response-strategy selection across
  domains. This version reports no experimental results.
type: dataset
